 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Fragments of a youth, far relieved from\nThe burden of this earth's harsh tyranny,\nSits upon the very walls of Heaven,\nAnd by his own name is called. 'Tis only\nThat he may be found; when Nature herself\nHath left him to her, what meaning is\nWhen she enkindles some animal fire,\nOr makes the wild flowers more tenderly bloom?\nHis soul shall yet remain immortal, and\nHe knows not whether they were his creation\nIn Gods' mould, or in our, neither can\nAscend into Heaven through Heaven.",
